WEBVTT

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:16.570
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:27.590
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:33.120
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.630
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:43.600
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:49.400
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:54.370
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.780
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:11.100
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:23.340
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.280
You disturber of peace through-
out the universe!

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.890
Not only do you deny the justice
that I am destined to defend...

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.800
...but you, Home Run Girl,
are my eternal rival!

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.800
Give me a break,
would you?

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.760
Today...

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:51.800
...we'll settle this
once and for all!

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.640
Anytime, Strike
Man!

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.510
Here goes!

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.780
This is the ball that embodies
the justice of my being.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.940
My deadly...

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.040
...Strike Big
Bang...

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.420
...Galaxy Meteor Crash
Ball of Justice!

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.060
Go ahead and
hit it...

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.130
...if you
can!

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.410
FILE. 25
RUN, STRIKE
MAN, RUN!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.920
M... My ball!

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:47.930
My deadly Strike Big Bang Galaxy
Meteor Crash Ball of Justice!

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.720
I win.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.160
Now will you do as promised and come
quietly with me down to the station?

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.330
But...

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.030
But... justice will
always prevail!

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.270
Huh?

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.430
That's right. I
am Justice!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.250
And because we are
one and the same...

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.970
...I cannot possibly
be defeated!

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.580
Next time, you won't
be so lucky.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:14.880
Until then, farewell,
Home Run Girl!

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.820
Huh?

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.930
Natsumi! We've got
to follow him.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.460
Oh! Yeah, right!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.930
Stop! You gave me your word!
You said you'd come quietly!

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.130
What?

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.270
Huh?

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.740
Just leave this
to me!

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.290
I... I don't believe
that guy!

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.000
Fear the power of my Strike
Air Leak Tactic!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.440
Justice will always
prevail!

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.900
There you go.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.720
Here.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:33.630
Thanks, Aoi.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.060
Thank you.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.570
Not at all.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.570
I'm exhausted.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:39.870
Me, too.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.470
Hey girls!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.010
Hello hello hello!!

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.880
Ahhh! Leave us alone!

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.250
Hmm?

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.380
Hmm?
Well...

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.980
...it's not all
that bad.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:55.820
See?

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:56.960
What's that?

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.250
The evening edition.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.760
"Strike Man..."

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.260
"...vs. Homerun Girl, Police Officer"

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:04.400
"24 losses, 0 ties"

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:10.600
What's this? "Strike Man
sighted in Bokuto Park."

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.800
"Vanquished by
Home Run Girl...

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.640
"...a policewoman from
Bokuto Station."

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.210
Unreal! You're famous,
Natsumi!

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.610
Usually the only ones who
make it to the papers...

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.480
...are people who've done
something bad.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.090
Is that supposed to make me feel better?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.680
Oh come on, stop being so shy.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.590
Hmm?

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.690
Take care of that, will you?
Okay, okay!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.420
All right.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.860
Her style's looking more and more...
Get me out of this thing!

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.540
...like Strike Man's.
Please! I'll be good!

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:41.670
Please! I'll be good!

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:42.830
I see what you mean.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:43.500
What?!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.010
"Karaoke Pub"
What?!

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.910
"Karaoke Pub"

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:52.010
Thanks. 'Night.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.870
Thanks again.
Take care.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:57.620
<i>I think I'm in love!</i>

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.820
"Karaoke Room"

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:06.490
Can't wait to
hit the hay.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:07.560
Huh?

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.560
A flat tire!

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:14.500
Oh, no!

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.730
Huh? What the?!

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:24.110
"Don't drink and drive!"

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:29.140
You're old enough to know the difference
between right and wrong.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.610
That sounds like a damsel
in distress!

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.920
Help me!

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.290
What happened?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.620
A creepy guy is
following me!

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.660
What?!

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.860
Oh, my! Aren't you the
famous Strike Man?!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.730
One and the same,
my pretty damsel.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.140
Stop!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:52.760
Huh?

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.370
You won't
get away!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:55.900
Wha?

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:01.240
You harasser of
pretty damsels!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:04.940
I, Strike Man, Defender of Justice,
will deal with you!

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.680
You won't get away!

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.460
Stay here, out
of danger.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.690
My deadly Super Justice Energy
"Spring Has Come" Ball!

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.590
Look out!

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.470
Foolish man. I knew
he'd try to get away.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.600
By the way, my pretty
damsel...

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.910
Why did you tell him
to look out?

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.240
Uh...

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.290
Because... well...

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.410
Hmm?

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:42.680
Because I...

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:47.250
I wanted to help you,
Strike Man!

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:51.360
I figured that if he
spun around...

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.760
...your Ball of Justice would hit
him squarely on the face.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.500
Aha! Just as
I thought!

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:01.140
My pretty damsel, you truly understand
the importance of Justice!

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.470
Perhaps there is still hope
left for the world!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.770
Will you join me...

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.580
...in giving this dastardly villain
a heaping helping of justice?

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:11.490
What?!

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.650
Come on!

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:13.850
Wait a minute!

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.820
Huh?

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:21.490
There's someone much more
evil than this man.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.260
Oh?! More evil?!

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:38.900
<i>"Well, actually...</i>

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:42.070
<i>"...my father borrowed some money</i>
<i>from a terrible place."</i>

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.980
<i>"He was a day late paying</i>
<i>back the money."</i>

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.780
<i>"So they came</i>
<i>to me and..."</i>

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.750
<i>Say no more, my</i>
<i>pretty damsel.</i>

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.390
<i>Where is this place?</i>

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.260
This is it.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:03.770
"Loan Company"

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:10.740
Ow! Ow!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.680
How dare that jerk
get me like this.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:17.210
But thanks to him, everything's
going just as planned.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.810
He believed every
word I said.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:21.750
Idiot.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:24.720
His twisted logic has
convinced him that...

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:29.850
...the best way to punish a
crooked moneylender...

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.730
...is to take his money and give it
back to his damsel in distress.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:36.790
So he'll be stealing
the money for us.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.770
But that's not how
he'll see it.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.240
After all, he's a hero, the
Defender of Justice.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.870
That's some hero,
all right!

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:54.810
"Greetings."

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.890
"I am the Strike Man...

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.650
"...and I have come to obtain justice
for those people with loans...

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:04.000
"...who have been tortured
by this company."

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:09.040
What?!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:09.870
"Traffic Section"

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:13.000
The Strike Man is planning
a robbery?
"Traffic Section"

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.770
Are you sure there hasn't
been some mistake?

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:19.070
Well... I can't tell one
way or the other.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:23.010
I'd like to hear your opinions, seeing
as you're the experts on him.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.710
We are not the experts
on him.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:26.850
That's right.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.550
W... What I meant was you
understand him...

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:32.990
...you're his rivals for eternity.
No? I mean...

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.460
You're his friends,
well no, I mean...

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.030
...his kindred
spirits...

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.220
...not even close?
Uh...

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.300
At any rate, I'd like to ask
for your cooperation.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.500
Thank you.

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.910
"Loan Company"

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.000
There's got to be someone
else behind this.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:55.010
That sign was definitely the
work of the Strike Man.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:58.510
But something about
this seems different.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.550
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:02.620
His M.O. is totally
different.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:07.560
He's so simple-minded, somebody
could be playing him for a fool.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.130
And if that's
the case...

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:12.260
...he's not an accomplice,
but rather he's a puppet.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.930
We'll have to hunt down the
ones who are behind this.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.500
Aha! There he is!

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.410
I can't believe he's got the balls to walk
around in that get-up in broad daylight.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:24.740
Then I wonder if there really
is someone else involved?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.550
You're going to pay...

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:30.810
...you bloodsuckers!

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.160
He's going in!

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.850
All units stand by until
further notice.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.190
Roger!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.530
Excuse me!

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:48.190
I'm looking
for justice!

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:49.700
Welcome!

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.200
Uh? Umm...

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.470
Please! Have
a seat!

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.440
Th... Thank you. Thank
you very much.

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.440
Now how may I help
you today, sir?

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:03.950
Uh... well... I'd like
all of your money.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.180
Yes, sir. Right
away, sir.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.150
Sorry to keep you
waiting, sir.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:13.560
Here's all the money we
have at this branch.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:14.630
Oh?

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.600
Thank you very
much.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:22.430
Do come again.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.970
Is this really an evil
moneylender?

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:35.440
The Defender of Justice cannot
allow himself to be indecisive!

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.550
Everything's going
according to plan.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:46.190
Roger.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:47.690
There he goes.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.300
He's heading toward
the 3rd district.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.660
Gotcha.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.190
The transmitter in the suitcase
seems to be working.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:58.160
Yoriko's back with me.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.830
Just hang on a minute,
all right?

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.480
Natsumi! Let's see if we can track
down the people behind this.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:04.340
Okay.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:13.350
Hang on, my pretty damsel!
I'm on my way!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.860
Even one of those cases
would be enough for us.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.450
And as soon as we get our hands
on it, we'll get out of here.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:26.360
Then he'll be left standing there
to be caught red-handed.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:29.770
Hmm?

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:32.300
Mr. Strike Man!

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:32.870
Oh!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.000
My pretty damsel!

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.370
Oh! My pretty damsel!

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:39.940
Hey...

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:43.450
...weren't we supposed to meet
further up, by the riverbank?

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:44.680
Sorry...

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:48.310
...I just couldn't wait any longer
to see if you'd made it all right!

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:51.390
What a pure and innocent
heart you have...

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:12.910
My pretty damsel.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:15.910
Yes?

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:19.650
You forgot about these
two cases!

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:24.920
Hey!

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.820
What about these
other two?!

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:29.350
They must be the people
behind this!

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.190
Natsumi, you take care
of Strike Man.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.200
Leave him to me!

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.430
Hey!

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.070
Hurry up! Step
on it!

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:39.210
I know, I know!

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.500
Hey!

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:42.310
Thank you very much!

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.610
What?!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.680
Stop! Thief!

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:48.910
What gives you the right to
call other people thieves?!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.290
Stop where you are!

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.950
Wait a minute, aren't you
the Home Run Girl?!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.920
Who you calling
Home Run Girl?!

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.220
I knew it!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.300
I've lured out the
Strike Man.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:03.930
Roger.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:07.160
I'll give you the location of the culprits
as soon as I can pinpoint it.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:09.200
Yeah, just make
it fast.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.200
I will. Anyway, Yoriko and
Aoi are hot on their trail.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.540
This is despicable!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:19.010
Home Run Girl, you were
a thief all along!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.610
Give me
a break!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:21.200
Huh?

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.780
Are you all right,
lady?

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.110
What's that?

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:33.080
Good always has
the last laugh!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.320
Natsumi! Pass!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.120
Here!

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:40.530
Aah! The Strike Man's
following us!

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.100
I'm not surprised.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.060
Yoriko! Make a right...

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.400
...and head for the
Taihei District.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:47.700
Huh?!

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:51.330
The roads are narrow
up there! I'll get lost!

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.170
What are you saying?!

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:56.510
We have to lead the Strike Man to their
hide-out so he can see for himself...

00:15:56.620 --> 00:16:00.580
...that they used him
for their robbery!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.220
All right. I understand.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:04.690
Stop right there!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.560
I need that money to bring justice
to an innocent victim!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.190
Uh...

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:13.700
Yoriko! That's the
wrong street!

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:14.890
You're on a
one-way!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.700
I'm lost!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:17.840
Yoriko!

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.700
Okay, take the
next left.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.510
It's too narrow! I'll never
make it down there!

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.200
Oh, jeez.

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:27.670
I'll have to keep
going straight!

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.110
<i>So...</i>

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:32.410
<i>... even the police have been</i>
<i>backing the Home Run Girl!</i>

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:33.680
<i>It's unforgivable!</i>

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:39.190
It's a dead end!

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.320
What do we
do now?!

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:42.790
Stop...

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:46.060
...you evil minions of
the Home Run Girl!

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:51.490
Run, Yoriko! Run!

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:55.570
Why don't we stop running away
and just arrest the guy?!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:57.570
Stop where you are!

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:03.570
Strike Jump!

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.080
Strike Grab!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.200
Home Run Girl!

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:20.630
Strike one, masked man.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:23.600
I get it.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.170
This has to be
the hide-out.

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:33.180
Stop! Home Run Girl!

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.950
You can't escape me,
Home Run Girl!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.640
It's time to settle the score
once and for all!

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:39.810
Home Run Girl!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.150
I hate that.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:42.910
Give me a break and stop
calling me that!

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:43.920
What the?!

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:46.420
"Liquidation Sale!"

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:50.090
No way!

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.530
Umm... Aha!

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:54.830
What?!

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.300
Running is good
for the health!

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:06.780
I am honored that you
are my true rival!

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:08.750
That makes me
very happy!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.040
That makes
one of us.

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.260
Found it.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.230
Got one side open.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.240
How much do you
think it is?

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:36.740
Judging by the size, it's
bound to be millions!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.980
All thanks to
Strike Man!

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:41.270
Yeah.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:45.150
I never thought he'd
be that easy to fool.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:46.980
"Mr. Strike Man!"

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:49.120
"Oh! My pretty damsel!"

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:51.890
What an idiot!

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.530
You've got nowhere to
go, Home Run Girl!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.360
Now give me back
that money!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.270
If you want it so bad, then
come and get it!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.810
Then here I come!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.190
M... My pretty damsel!

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:29.820
It's counterfeit!

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.290
This, too?!

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:34.760
What's the meaning
of this?

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.770
To think that the loan company
uses counterfeit bills...

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.910
You've been tricked,
Strike Man!

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:46.000
Those two tricked you!

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.540
Oh, Home Run Girl!

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.810
I totally forgot
about you!

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:54.180
I told you to stop
calling me that.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:56.910
You've been taken
advantage of.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.820
I have?!

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.130
Now I know what
happened.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:06.220
These counterfeit bills were made
by you, Home Run Girl!

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:07.830
Why would I do that?!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:11.330
Figure it out! You've
been used by them!

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:15.070
You've been assisting
criminals!

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:18.570
You think I can be tricked by
this counterfeit money?

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:21.180
You're not even making
any sense!

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.580
Now be quiet and come down
to the station with us.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.440
What?!

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:26.580
We have a score to settle,
Home Run Girl!

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:35.560
All right. Let's go.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.660
Are they at
it again?

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.530
This time you've got to promise to
come down to the station if I win.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.170
Yeah.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.170
Come on!

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:47.100
Here we go!

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:54.580
You disturber of peace through-
out the universe.

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:57.680
You're the one disturbing
the peace.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:01.150
This ball embodies Justice,
Love, and Friendship...

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:06.450
...hit it if you can!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.190
You hit it.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.990
I win.

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.700
Now let's go down
to the station.

00:21:20.270 --> 00:21:23.570
What do you want to keep
doing this for, anyway?

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:26.200
I always win. It'll be a gazillion
years before you ever beat me.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:27.640
Natsumi! Natsumi!

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:28.780
Huh?

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:29.400
Ah!

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:32.980
I'll let you get away
with it this time!

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:37.050
But you'd better practice for
the next time we meet!

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:39.150
Natsumi.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.620
Get out of
my life!

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:50.190
Good always
triumphs!

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:11.420
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:20.030
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:31.040
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:39.150
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:47.950
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:56.800
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:04.370
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:14.090
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:17.190
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:25.160
"An Approaching Shadow"

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:28.020
A man...

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:31.330
...creeps towards you, keeping to
the shadows, at a fancy party.

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:33.170
In his hand, he holds a sharp knife.

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:35.010
Oh, stop! Stop! I'm scared!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:36.940
You're not the one being chased!

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:38.680
But I'm scared of stalkers!

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:40.480
Don't worry, Nakajima will
be coming along with us.

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:42.080
In that case, you should
be worried!

00:23:42.250 --> 00:23:44.110
Just what do you
mean by that?!

00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:46.180
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 26...

00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:48.350
..."A Red Dress And A Knife."

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:50.420
Kobayakawa, run!
